+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: `toml_edit` and `toml`
+
+Tests were added with `hegeltest` 0.28.2 across two sessions, in three places,
+per the skill's "modify existing test files" rule:
+
+- `crates/toml_edit/src/encode.rs` — the two existing proptest tests, ported to hegel
+  (the `proptest` dev-dependency was removed from `toml_edit`; `toml_writer`'s own
+  proptest usage is untouched).
+- `crates/toml_edit/tests/testsuite/edit.rs` — sixteen hegel tests (thirteen property
+  tests, two stateful model tests, one deterministically-failing bug pin) and their
+  generators, including a generator family for *valid TOML text* transcribed from the
+  TOML ABNF.
+- `crates/toml/tests/testsuite/value.rs` — three hegel tests for the `toml` crate's
+  serde-based `Value` round-trip and parser robustness.
+
+## Properties tested
+
+| # | Property | Test | Evidence |
+|---|----------|------|----------|
+| 1 | Any `String` put into a `Value` encodes to TOML that parses back to the same string (control characters must be escaped). | `encode::test::parseable_string` (src/encode.rs) | Existing proptest test of the same name. Ported per `porting.md`; generator broadened from `\PC*` (no control chars) to full `text()`, and strengthened from "parses" to round-trip equality (superset of the original property). |
+| 2 | Any `String` used as a `Key` encodes to TOML that parses back to the same key. | `encode::test::parseable_key` (src/encode.rs) | Existing proptest test; same broadening/strengthening as #1. |
+| 3 | Round-trip: `Value::from(i64)` → display → parse → `as_integer()` is identity across the full `i64` range, including `MIN`/`MAX`. | `edit::integer_value_roundtrip` | `From<i64> for Value` + `FromStr for Value`; catalogue "Roundtrip"/"Boundary" (precision loss through f64 is a listed bug pattern). |
+| 4 | Round-trip: `Value::from(f64)` → display → parse is bit-identical for non-NaN (including ±inf and −0.0), NaN stays NaN. | `edit::float_value_roundtrip` | `impl ValueRepr for f64` in src/encode.rs; `floats()` defaults include NaN/inf per the rust reference. |
+| 5 | Round-trip: `Value::from(Datetime)` → display → parse is identity for all four documented datetime forms, with field ranges taken from `toml_datetime`'s doc comments (incl. optional seconds, nanoseconds, leap years, ±23:59 offsets). | `edit::datetime_value_roundtrip` + composite `arbitrary_datetime` | Doc comments on `Datetime`/`Date`/`Time`/`Offset` in `toml_datetime/src/datetime.rs`; `impl ValueRepr for Datetime` in src/encode.rs. |
